   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( p(x) = \\sqrt{\\frac{x + 1}{4}} \\) and \\( q(x) = \\frac{x}{3} - 3 \\). The shaded region R shown is bounded by the graphs of p and q and the x-axis. By integrating with respect to y, find the exact area of R.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         46,
         3
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Solve each equation for x: \\( x = 4 y^{2} - 1 \\) from the graph of p, with \\( y \\ge 0 \\), and \\( x = 3 y + 9 \\) from the graph of q.",
         "rule_named": "rewrite each curve as a function of y"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The curves meet where \\( 4 y^{2} - 1 = 3 y + 9 \\), at \\( y = 2 \\), and the region runs from the x-axis, \\( y = 0 \\), up to there. On that interval the line is to the right of the parabola.",
         "rule_named": "limits in y and the right-hand curve"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The area is \\( \\int_{0}^{2} \\left(\\left(3 y + 9\\right) - \\left(4 y^{2} - 1\\right)\\right)\\,dy = \\frac{46}{3} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            46,
            3
         ],
         "rule_named": "area integral in y"
      }
   ],
